{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "about": "Example software watch list. Home Hub watches these for versions and update candidates; a site keeps its own list in local/software-watch.json (it replaces this file). Each item has one upstream (where the newest version is read) and one detect entry per machine id from site.json (how the installed version is read there, and where it was installed from). A detect entry may override the upstream when that machine installs the tool through another channel. Detect kinds: brew (formula in /opt/homebrew/opt), cask (Caskroom), app (bundle Info.plist), cmd (run a binary, read its version line), pydist (Python dist-info in a site-packages glob), json (version field of a JSON file). launchd names the job whose PID shows whether the service is running. inventory (optional) lists the data/knowledge.json entry ids this detect entry describes on that machine, for entries the inventory map cannot match by id or name (public/inventory-versions.js). NAS apps, Docker containers and the operating systems are discovered automatically and need no entry here.",
 "categories": {"ai": "AI runtimes", "agents": "Coding agents and apps", "infra": "Servers and infrastructure", "tools": "Toolchain"},
 "items": [
  {"id": "llama.cpp", "name": "llama.cpp", "category": "ai", "scheme": "llamacpp", "upstream": {"type": "github", "repo": "ggml-org/llama.cpp", "tagPattern": "^v?\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$"}, "detect": {"studio": {"kind": "brew", "formula": "llama.cpp", "upstream": {"type": "brew-formula", "name": "llama.cpp"}}, "mini": {"kind": "brew", "formula": "llama.cpp", "upstream": {"type": "brew-formula", "name": "llama.cpp"}}, "mini_server": {"kind": "cmd", "path": "~/llama.cpp/build/bin/llama-server", "args": "--version", "match": "version: (\\S+)", "launchd": "com.example.llama-server", "inventory": ["llama-server"], "source": {"label": "Built from source"}}}},
